From 35d4ff3f43ad839952466d7d8580320adba95b8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:16:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: seed the dead-unique table with uniques at start-up

borg_init_flow_kill() fills borg_race_death[] from r_info[].max_num,
which the game sets to 0 for a unique the player has killed.  The test
is inverted against its own comment ("Skip non-uniques"): it skips the
uniques and checks the non-uniques, whose max_num is never 0, so the
table starts empty even when the savefile records dead uniques.

The first borg_update() pass fills the table on its new-level branch,
but borg_think() calls borg_notice() before borg_update() and then
computes borg.power from that notice.  On the first pass after the
borg starts, borg.power therefore misses the dead-unique terms (for
example Sauron's death in borg_power()), while every candidate the
same pass evaluates (items to wear, junk to drop) is scored with the
table filled.  A candidate that is no better, or worse, can then
outscore the stale baseline: the borg swaps in a weaker item or drops
and ignores a useful one.

Skip non-uniques, as the comment and the matching scan in
borg_update() do.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#101.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
index 0c347c5ad..e914ea7fb 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
@@ -3327,7 +3327,7 @@ void borg_init_flow_kill(void)
             continue;
 
         /* Skip non-uniques */
-        if (rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_UNIQUE))
+        if (!rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_UNIQUE))
             continue;
 
         /* Mega-Hack -- Access "dead unique" list */
